      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "We aimed to review the literature linking metabolic factors to Diffuse Idiopathic Skeletal Hyperostosis (DISH), in order to assess associations between growth factors and DISH."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "We identified studies in our personal database and PubMed using the following keywords in various combinations: \"diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis\", \"ankylosing hyperostosis\", \"Forestier's disease\", \"diabetes\", \"insulin\", \"obesity\", \"metabolic\", \"growth factors\", \"adipokines\", \"glucose tolerance\" and \"chondrocytes\"."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "We were not able to do a systematic review due to variability in methodology of studies. We found positive associations between obesity (especially abdominal obesity), Type 2 diabetes mellitus, glucose intolerance, hyperinsulinemia and DISH."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Current research indicates that certain metabolic factors associate with DISH. More precise studies deriving from these findings on these and other newly identified bone-growth factors are needed."
        }
      ]},
